  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "uniequip_001_folnic",
      "name": {
        "en": "Folinic's Badge",
        "zh": "亚叶证章",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "INITIAL",
      "typeName2": "",
      "icon": "uniequip_001_folnic",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operator Folinic has demonstrated a remarkable aptitude for healing teammates in the field.\nThe Field Operations Department has thus passed the following resolution:\nThis operator shall be appointed a Medic Operator during field operations to exercise Medic responsibilities.\nIn witness whereof,\nThis badge is hereby conferred upon the above named.",
        "zh": "干员亚叶擅长在战场上为干员提供治疗\n根据外勤部门决议\n在外勤任务中划分为医疗干员，行使医师职责\n特别颁发此证章\n以兹证明",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uniequip_002_folnic",
      "name": {
        "en": "Mother's Cravat",
        "zh": "母亲的领巾",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "ADVANCED",
      "typeName2": "Y",
      "icon": "uniequip_002_folnic",
      "description": {
        "en": "After finishing her studies, on the first day at her new post, Folinic picked out a light blue cravat for herself, its color much like that of medical gloves, seemingly chosen with little hesitation. With her outfit all together and a thrice-over in the mirror, she took her papers and tools with her, off to what was now her position in the Rhodes Island Medical Department.\nIt was an uneventful day. She got seated at her workplace, met Atro and the rest of her colleagues, set up her itinerary, went to a meeting, ate lunch, wrangled all manner of IDs, confirmed the laboratory she'd be using, ate dinner, chatted with Professor Kal'tsit, and went to read in the library. That was it, sunup to sundown.\nHowever, a subtlety to Kal'tsit's actions weighed on her mind. When she looked at Folinic, her eyes seemed inadvertently drawn to her cravat. Folinic had met with Kal'tsit several times throughout the day, and almost every time she did that, as small as it was, to the point she'd thought she was wearing it wrong, and that was how Kal'tsit was opting to notify her. Yet when she got back to her dorm and stood in front of her mirror, she found the cravat still tied neat and tidily upon her chest.\nIf something was wrong, Professor Kal'tsit would've mentioned it on the spot, Folinic thought. She untied her cravat, then tied it once again.\nSo, what exactly was the issue?\nFolinic puzzled over it, and in short order took it off, only to put it back on slowly this time, once again remembering how her mother taught her to tie it—\nA choked gasp escaped her throat before she covered her mouth. Folinic was a very disciplined person, but at this very moment, she was losing control over herself.\nShe tried to hold back her voice, but managed only to sob in heavier, more broken fits, almost suffocating.\nEven standing up straight felt beyond her, and her hands could barely brace against the table before she fell to the ground, where she curled into a ball.\nRationale? Wisdom? What use were they?\nAching—weeping—these were all she had left.\nA pain that a single night could hardly quell.\nHow long must it take, until you finally move past losing family so close to you, and all the inexhaustible grief—how long until you finally forget?\n......\nAt dawn the next day, Folinic came to on the ice-cold floor. She wiped her tears dry, went to the bathroom, and ran a cold shower. As the bracing water struck her back, she planned in her head to open up more possibilities in her own work.\nJust before she left, she picked out a jet-black cravat for herself.",
        "zh": "在结束学业，正式到岗的第一天，亚叶为自己选了一块浅蓝色的领巾，它的颜色和医用手套很相近，亚叶在选这块领巾时几乎没怎么犹豫。在搭配好服饰，在镜子前检查了三次着装后，她带上资料与工具，前往罗德岛医疗部内属于她的工位。\n那是个没什么波澜的日子。她坐上工位，认识了安托与其他同事，建立日程，参加会议，吃午饭，办理各种证件，确认后续将要使用的实验室，吃晚饭，和凯尔希老师聊天，去图书馆看书。一天就这样过去了。\n然而凯尔希有个细微的举动令亚叶十分在意，当她看向自己的时候，凯尔希似乎总会不经意地瞟一眼她的领巾。在这一天里，她见过凯尔希数次，几乎每次凯尔希都会有这样的小动作。她甚至以为是自己没佩戴好所以凯尔希在以这种方式提醒她。可当亚叶回到宿舍站在镜子前时，领巾依旧端端正正地系在她胸前。\n如果有问题，凯尔希老师一定会当场提出。亚叶这么想着。她解下领巾，重新系了一遍。\n那么，到底是哪里出了差错？\n亚叶疑惑着，随后解下领巾，放慢动作，回忆着母亲教她系领巾的动作，重新——\n在捂住嘴之前，一声急促的哽咽就已经从喉中传了出来。亚叶是个很自律的人，但她现在失去了对自己的控制。\n她想忍着不出声，却只能在抽泣到近乎窒息后哭得更凶。\n她连站都站不直，抓着桌沿的手也没能支撑多久，很快地，她就只能倒在地上蜷缩成一团。\n思考、理智，能有什么用？\n疼痛与哭泣，她就只剩下这些了。\n一个夜晚不足以消解这种苦痛。\n至于遗忘，时间又要耗费多久，才能化解这种失去至亲的无尽悲伤？\n……\n第二天清晨，亚叶从冰冷的地板上醒来。她擦干眼泪，去浴室洗了个冷水澡，当冷水打在脊背上的时候，她心中盘算着为自己多加些工作的可能性。\n临出门前，她为自己选了块纯黑的领巾。",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ],
